x86_64-windows  a handler in this case ends with `return`, and on this target a handler is a funclet - leaving one early means handing back the address to carry on at in the register a return value would travel in, which is not built yet. The class-typed throw it also needs landed for this target on 2026-09-26 (throw-class-pointer-ms.cpp runs here); try-catch.notarget records the return refusal from the other side.
